 "version": 1,
 "title": "Industrial Drum Loop",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: a pounding, four-on-the-floor industrial beat: a hard kick on every beat, a crushed, metallic snare on 2 and 4, ticking hats on the sixteenths, all a little distorted. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: the Clock drives everything. Kick: a sine whose pitch an envelope drops fast (FM), on every BEAT. Snare: noise through a band-pass plus a low triangle for body, mixed and Crushed, triggered by a Sequencer stepping on eighths with only steps 3 and 7 on (beats 2 and 4). Hats: noise through a high-pass, on every 1/16. A Mixer, Drive and a short Reverb glue it.\n\nTweak: TEMPO; the kick's pitch envelope DECAY (a longer drop booms); the snare's BITS; switch sequencer steps on for extra snares; the drum mixer's levels; DRIVE.",
